ow push-ins on the close-ups, one slow pull-back at the end, no fast cuts, no whip pans, slight natural breathing motion.\n\nAudio: kettle whistling softly with rising pitch, coffee pouring in a steady stream, ceramic mug clinking on the counter, faint birdsong through the window, floorboard creaking once under the cat's paws, a clear cat meow at 6s, a soft piano melody underneath, closing with a gentle chord at 9s.\n\nNo text, subtitles, logos or watermarks of any kind, no animation or cartoon rendering, no extra limbs or morphing, no flickering objects, no overly-CG look, keep the live-action texture.\n",
